- Build incident (6.1.31 superseded by 6.1.32): the first SLF4J2 build regressed TestLog4j2 with a StackOverflowError. genLog4j2.py rewrote every "emit(level, marker, " in the SimpleLogBuilder template to "emit2(" - a blanket string replace that also rewrote the body of emit2 itself, turning it into infinite self-recursion (LoggerClass$SimpleLogBuilder.emit2 at LoggerClass.java:2292). Fixed by protecting the emit2 body from the rewrite: _tail() substitutes a placeholder for "emit(level, marker, slf4jMarkerPrefix + message, t);" before the rewrite and restores it afterwards, so the 22 fluent log() methods call emit2 and emit2 alone calls emit
- Threshold semantics of the SLF4J 2.0 fluent gate fixed: the engine probes are exact-level (LEVEL == LEVEL_<X>) so only the configured level reports true. atX() and isEnabledForLevel(Level) originally relied on those probes, which made atWarn()/atError() return the NOOP builder under Level=INFO (fluent error cases wrote nothing) and isEnabledForLevel(WARN) report false. Both now derive the enabled threshold from whichever probe is on and compare with the official Level integers (ERROR=40, WARN=30, INFO=20, DEBUG=10, TRACE=0), matching the official threshold semantics: at Level=INFO, atInfo()/atWarn()/atError() build live events, atDebug()/atTrace() return NOOP
- Verification: javap audit 0 missing official methods for every family; ApiUsageSample dual-compiles OK against the official jars and against the replacement jar; TestSlf4j 14/14 (six new 2.0 cases all pass); TestLog4j2 back to 8/8; full TestAll 63 passed / 0 failed (9/6/8/6/5/14/8/7)
